    "id": "p10-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Write down the first few terms of the GP generated by substituting the positive integers into the exponential function $f(x)=\\frac{4}{25}\\times5^x$. Then write down a formula for the $n$th term.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac45,\\ 4,\\ 20,\\ 100,\\ldots$\n\n$a_n=\\frac{4}{25}\\times5^n$, for $n=1,2,3,\\ldots$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(1)&=\\frac{4}{25}\\times5=\\frac45\\\\f(2)&=\\frac{4}{25}\\times25=4\\\\f(3)&=\\frac{4}{25}\\times125=20\\\\f(4)&=\\frac{4}{25}\\times625=100\\end{align*}$$\nGeometric sequences are equivalent to exponential functions, with the domain restricted to positive whole numbers.\n$$a_n=\\frac{4}{25}\\times5^n,\\qquad n=1,2,3,\\ldots.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 31
  },
